{"title":"Butterfly Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Midpoint\" title=\"Midpoint\">midpoint</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chord\" title=\"Chord\">chord</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a>, through which two other chords <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are drawn. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersect chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. The <b>Butterfly Theorem</b> states that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:528px-Butterfly_theorem.svg.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/97/528px-Butterfly_theorem.svg.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"528\" height=\"483\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Butterfly_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This simple proof uses <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Projective_geometry\" title=\"Projective geometry\">projective geometry</a>.\n</p><p>First we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8fa27a516ebab317245edeba70e71fec72775c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(AP, AB; AD, AQ) = (CP, CB; CD, CQ).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"333\" height=\"20\" />\nTherefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76f14d734cf4f6f44a177ce4a3e7f24c3fbf473b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(PX)(MQ)}{(PQ)(MX)} = \\frac{(PM)(YQ)}{(PQ)(YM)}.\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"43\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/847193b78b9752a76660d2f53b257087d210f6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MQ = PM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57417825869128252443c99dc7976d36cc3c8a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{MX}{YM} = \\frac{XP}{QY}.\\]\" width=\"100\" height=\"40\" />\nMoreover,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c2977f9ff304e1aa22ec55c7a3b4fa11b6509d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{MX + PX}{YM + QY} = 1,\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"40\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/911147b9d1154ec8c7d3187ec3418f0052d32638.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MX = YM,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" /> as desired.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Related_Reading\">Related Reading</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Butterfly_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Related Reading\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://agutie.homestead.com/FiLEs/GeometryButterfly.html\">http://agutie.homestead.com/FiLEs/GeometryButterfly.html</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~fritsch/butterfly.pdf\">http://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~fritsch/butterfly.pdf</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Butterfly_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Midpoint\" title=\"Midpoint\">Midpoint</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018074944\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.032 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 104/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3197/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7830:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018074944 and revision id 66983. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}